{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqelk8e5ths","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Context Verdict Model scope: all three context edge types (note-note, note-task, task-task)","summary":"The Context Verdict Model (CVM, replacing \"edge-classifier\") must learn verdicts for all three context edge types: (1) note→note (knowledge overlap), (2) note→task (knowledge relevance to work item), (3) task→task (sibling work context). Renamed from \"edge-classifier\" / \"edge verdict model\" to \"context verdict model\" to distinguish from the prompt classifier pipeline. The judge already seeds task→task candidates (Judge B, 091a4bf1/15). V1 model underrepresents task→task because task embeddings were sparse before the native task lifecycle pipeline (task #8) landed. V2 refit: after sufficient task→task verdicts accumulate with real cosine scores (not zero-fallback), re-run featurizer + fit. Featurizer already captures note_a_kind/note_b_kind features — no schema changes needed for v2, just more training data. Blocking edges (kind:blocking) are structural/explicit and bypass the CVM entirely — the CVM only adjudicates context edges.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T02:31:33.245Z","vec":[-0.018473606556653976,-0.024579690769314766,-0.0381300114095211,-0.020612619817256927,0.10404722392559052,0.014186442829668522,0.01760558970272541,0.028801949694752693,-0.03524569794535637,-0.030198432505130768,-0.0035770991817116737,-0.0675647109746933,0.005305522587150335,0.03524162620306015,-0.00034613790921866894,0.028036711737513542,0.12883107364177704,-0.04466598853468895,-0.034931574016809464,0.011780921369791031,0.0629243329167366,0.021457768976688385,0.02635745145380497,-0.01914820820093155,-0.04206939414143562,0.042735107243061066,-0.0933498665690422,0.016428833827376366,0.02595134824514389,-0.057492807507514954,0.025547286495566368,0.056058794260025024,0.025048386305570602,0.04582977294921875,0.039054837077856064,0.03459002822637558,-0.02749382145702839,0.018